// Phase 08 Task 2(a) -- composition depth >= 2 (D-08-28.2), ACCEPTING member.
// Twin of relay_depth2_refuse.lang: caller's own body is byte-identical
// (verified by structural comparison in check_test.go). leaf declares an
// OWNED return (`-> Buffer`, body `let taken = take buffer; taken`) instead
// of a borrow; relay forwards leaf's owned result directly (no local borrow
// needed -- relay's own declared return is also plain `-> Buffer`, an
// ordinary owned pass-through, needing no origin declaration at all).
// `check.Program` (package check alone) admits this program with zero
// diagnostics -- the composition-depth-2 refusal above is contract-driven at
// EVERY hop, not merely at depth 1.
//
// D-12-04c CORRECTION (2026-09-12, recorded per D-09-45 -- never silently
// fixed): this header used to claim the KNOWN RESIDUAL below still held --
// that corevalidate ALSO refuses this fixture with core.move_while_borrowed
// even though check's own interprocedural law correctly admits it. That
// claim is STALE and was VERIFIED NO LONGER TRUE by Phase 12's pre-flight
// probe (12-CONTEXT.md D-12-04a/D-12-04c): corevalidate.Valid == true on
// this unmodified fixture. The closing decision is Phase 09's D-09-03,
// which deliberately retired this fixture (and twin_a_accept.lang) from
// session_peer_gate_test.go's peerDivergenceExpected register -- the
// register's own retirement comment says so, but this fixture's own header
// was never updated to match, until now. The probe's first draft pinned
// D-10-C01 against this fixture expecting the old divergence and went red
// for exactly this reason: the fixture was not wrong, the header was.
//
// ORIGINAL (superseded) KNOWN RESIDUAL text, quoted verbatim so the
// correction is auditable rather than silently erased: "see
// twin_a_accept.lang's header. The full `lang check` CLI additionally
// consults corevalidate.Validate once `check` itself passes; corevalidate's
// own loan-liveness re-derivation is still intraprocedural (unmodified this
// phase, Phase 09's own charter) and unconditionally treats an OpCall's
// target as inheriting every loan its SourceID carries, so it also refuses
// this fixture (core.move_while_borrowed) even though `check`'s own
// interprocedural law -- the one under test -- correctly admits it."

module phase08.relay_depth2_accept

export {
  fn caller
}

fn leaf(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let taken = take buffer
  taken
}

fn relay(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let forwarded = leaf(buffer)
  forwarded
}

fn caller(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let aliased = relay(borrowed)
  let delivered = take buffer
  aliased
}
